// A string something else holds is never freed or extended in place, whatever
// the function then does to its own name for it. Each function overwrites the
// name after the other holder has it, and the program prints what the holder
// sees: a wrong free (the guard poisons it) or a wrong append changes it.
//   stash  pushed k into a list
//   alias  named it b
// Freed: only the digit string of each first `+ n`, one per function, here and
// in b.id (4 in all).
stash(string[] box, int n) {
  string k = "k" + n;
  push(box, k);
  k = k + "!";
} return int n;

alias(int n) {
  string a = "a" + n;
  string b = a;
  a = a + "x";
} return string b;
